  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 354eb510ac5346f44864591bbf3f64c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Chapter1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ChapterData
  chapterNumber: 1
  chapterName: Landfall
  chapterDescription: "The Null-Vector has crash-landed on an uncharted world. Kyra-Dominia
    must establish the colony's foothold, harvest alien resources, and begin the
    Supreme Habitation Protocol. But the planet's indigenous defenders \u2014 the
    Lumina \u2014 will not watch their world be reformatted in silence."
  chapterIntroText: "The descent was never meant to end like this. A fatal miscalculation
    buried the Null-Vector nose-deep in the continent's mud, scattering cargo pods
    across the valley. As monsoon rains hammer the alien jungle, Kyra-Dominia surveys
    what remains \u2014 a functioning Command Center, a handful of task-bots, and
    an endless wilderness of crystalline rocks and hostile flora.\n\nMineral scans
    show iron deposits nearby. The reactor still hums. The Supreme Habitation Protocol
    can proceed.\n\nBut the ground trembles with something alive. The Lumina are
    watching. And every factory built, every tree overwritten, every plume of pollution
    that rises \u2014 it all draws them closer.\n\nEstablish the bastion. Harvest
    what you can. Build what you must. Genesis begins now."
  chapterOutroText: "The Warden collapses, its massive frame crashing into scorched
    earth with a tremor felt across the valley. For the first time since landfall,
    the jungle is silent.\n\nKyra-Dominia stands amid the wreckage of her first true
    battle. The colony holds. The Protocol continues. But as long-range sensors flicker
    to life, the readings beyond the mountains reveal something unexpected \u2014
    vast energy signatures, structures that predate even the Lumina by millennia.\n\nThis
    world has deeper secrets than its custodians. And now, it knows she is here."
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5414e7b715861ff479244f4f31951b27, type: 2}
